<title>UK: Fuji Bank sets $500 mln two-tranche bond.</title>
<headline>Fuji Bank sets $500 mln two-tranche bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche issue was announced by joint lead managers Fuji and Goldman Sachs International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   FUJI FINANCE CAYMAN LTD</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  FUJI BANK</p>
<p> TRANCHE A</p>
<p> AMT    $350 MLN	BASE	 6M-LIBOR  MATURITY    PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN   **+90 BP    PAY DATE    11.MAR.97</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  A3/=	ISS PRICE  PAR	 FULL FEES   75 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	**UNTIL YEAR FIVE, THEN 6M LIBOR +240 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	CALLABLE MARCH 2002</p>
<p>* * * *</p>
<p>TRANCHE B</p>
<p> AMT    $150 MLN	COUPON   **7.3	 MATURITY  **PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE   FIXED/FRN     ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    11.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  75 BP     SPREAD     +115 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	**CALLABLE 11.MAR.02 WHEN COUPON BECOMES 6M LIBOR</p>
<p>		+240 BP</p>
<p>* * * *</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 10-100</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP/CI</p>
<p> MGT/UND    50 BP     SELL CONC  25 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
